Install Windows 10 or Windows 11 on a Raspberry Pi SD card.
This tool is a 100% legal way to use a supported Debian- or Ubuntu-based Linux operating system to flash a Raspberry Pi drive with the necessary files to run Windows 10 or 11.

Usage is simple:

- Choose an operating system version. (Windows 11, Windows 10, Custom version)
- Choose the Raspberry Pi model. (Pi 3, Pi 4, or Pi 5)
- Choose a language.
- Choose a storage drive to flash.
- Click Flash.

It's as simple as that. WoR-Flasher takes care of the rest - downloading or importing Windows, adding the required UEFI firmware and available drivers, writing the target drive, and verifying the result. When finished, WoR-Flasher will tell you exactly what to do next.

To run: Menu -> Accessories -> WoR-Flasher
To run the graphical interface in a terminal: ~/wor-flasher/install-wor-gui.sh
To run the command-line interface in a terminal: ~/wor-flasher/install-wor.sh

If you encounter problems, run WoR-Flasher in a terminal to capture errors. This Pi-Apps definition preserves Botspot's original project and community attribution.
